cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the article it accompanies (listed under references)."
type: software
title: "pit-multisource: point-in-time construction of a multisource dataset and reproduction of the article's results"
abstract: >-
  Rebuilds the point-in-time multisource dataset of Binance BTC/ETH bars, GDELT GKG news metadata
  and US release calendars from its sources, and reproduces the numbers of the article
  "Point-in-Time Consistency for Multisource Time-Series Data" from the released dataset. Every released table except the raw GKG records, the slot ledger and `news/gdelt_slots.parquet` is rebuilt from sources and compared row for row; GDELT selection is checked on a 30-slot sample of the original archives; the news and entity builds start from the released raw GKG records and the source-domain build from the released news records.
version: "1.0.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.CODE
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AndrewThanatos/pit-multisource"
authors:
